ITEM SYSTEM OVERVIEW:
ItemDatabase: Records a list of "ItemDefinitions" these keep track of names, icons, visual world appearances, etc.
Real items that exist in the game are "ItemInstances" that have a key that links them to an ItemDefinition, as well as
custom information like how many items are in the stack and any custom data an item might have (for example pelts have
a colour and quality).
Weapons have custom definitions called "WeaponDefinitions" that are extended from the normal "ItemDefinition" class. They
also need to be represented by an ItemInstance to exist in the world.
